# OCRT layered gas absorption cross section, 1 nm wavelength bins
# Gas: NO2
# Spectral range: 330-1100 nm, 1 nm; 40 AFGL US76 levels
# n_layers = 40
# 330-349 nm: HITRAN Vandaele XSC (220/294 K) relative spectral shape, linearly interpolated/clamped in T and anchored per layer to the canonical Bogumil-family value at 350 nm.
# 350-1100 nm: existing 5-temperature Bogumil/SCIAMACHY continuum-merged canonical LUT preserved exactly.
# No empirical wavelength-dependent correction: one scalar boundary normalization per atmospheric layer.
# Units: cm^2/molecule
# Layer order: ascending z_km (layer 0 = ground, layer 39 = TOA)
